  "id": "COMPOUND:30011 - PROTEIN:5942",
  "verbalization": "Nudiposide is implicated in the regulation of Tankyrase-2 through a multi-step pathway involving SNU-387. The evidence suggests that Nudiposide acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn targets Tankyrase-2. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple intermediates, including (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol and S-ethylcysteine zwitterion, all of which are linked to Tankyrase-2. The scores from the paths indicate a consistent and significant relationship, suggesting that Nudiposide may influence Tankyrase-2 through these intermediates. The mechanism appears to involve SNU-387 as a key mediator, potentially modulating Tankyrase-2 activity in a complex regulatory network. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of SNU-387 in linking Nudiposide to Tankyrase-2, emphasizing the importance of this intermediate in the drug-target relationship.",
